WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.070
Welcome, and thank you for observing
today.

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.243
Here is your role, your screen, notes,

3
00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:11.520
messages, and what to do if something goes
wrong.

4
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.180
You've already joined, with the join link
or code, as an Observer.

5
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.969
When the participants' briefing ends,

6
00:00:19.969 --> 00:00:24.060
the room screen shows the join code for
them to scan.

7
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:29.770
Remember: this exercise tests the plan,
not individuals.

8
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.199
You watch and take notes.

9
00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:40.000
You don't answer injects or guide the
team, even when they are stuck.

10
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.880
What you see becomes the report's
evidence.

11
00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:52.070
On a phone, there are three tabs:
Exercise, Notes and Messages.

12
00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:58.750
On a laptop, the exercise is on the left,
with Notes and Messages on the right.

13
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.945
Exercise shows what the room sees, what to
watch for,

14
00:01:02.945 --> 00:01:07.000
and each department's answer once it is
submitted.

15
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.971
To log a note, open Notes and tap the
type:

16
00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:18.160
Positive, Needs improvement, or Critical
gap.

17
00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.610
Check the department; it is filled in when
the inject names one.

18
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.990
Write a few sentences, and press Log note.

19
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.650
You can log as many notes as you need.

20
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:38.610
Prefer to speak? Tap the microphone,
speak, and tap it again.

21
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:44.890
Correct the words, then press Log note;
speaking alone never sends anything.

22
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.570
Note what the team did, and what the plan
says.

23
00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:54.500
Where there is no plan, note what the
inject asked for.

24
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.320
Never name a person.

25
00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:02.980
If something would stop the response
altogether, choose Critical gap.

26
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.220
Your note reaches the facilitator straight
away.

27
00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.674
To reach the facilitator, open Messages,

28
00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:18.530
tap a ready-made line such as Our room
needs more time, and press Send.

29
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.580
Or type your own message and press Send.

30
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.700
It goes for your room, not under your
name.

31
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.620
Replies stay at the top until you press
Got it or Reply.

32
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.510
Took a call, or locked your screen?

33
00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:43.330
Nothing is lost. The page catches up by
itself.

34
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:50.000
If your device restarts, open the same
link and press Continue on Welcome back.

35
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:56.040
Logged notes are saved, and an unfinished
note comes back on the same device.

36
00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.730
If a participant loses their page, tap
Show join code.

37
00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:05.940
Your screen fills with the code for them
to scan.

38
00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:12.300
When the exercise ends, please answer the
one-minute survey on your screen.

39
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.415
Your notes stay open for up to five hours,

40
00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:19.010
but it's best to log them while they're
fresh.

41
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:26.140
To recap. Watch, never guide, and log
notes with Log note.

42
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.540
Critical gap reaches the facilitator at
once.

43
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.300
Show join code helps anyone who loses
their page.

44
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:40.071
Please set your phone to Do Not Disturb,
not flight mode,

45
00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:44.060
and keep it plugged in if you can. Thank
you.

